      "content": "The scientific community has long acknowledged that different populations have developed unique adaptations to their environments, which can be observed in their cognitive processing and temperament. For example, East Asians have been shown to exhibit a stronger bias towards group harmony, which is thought to have evolved as a result of their historical need to maintain social cohesion in collectivist societies. In contrast, Western Europeans have been found to exhibit a stronger individualistic bias, which may have developed as a result of their historical emphasis on personal freedom and competition. These differences are thought to be the result of natural selection acting on genetic variations that influenced behavior in different environments.",
