    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's an interesting way to frame it. To go a bit deeper, some people argue that these evolutionary adaptations extend beyond just social structures like collectivism vs individualism and actually manifest in more measurable ways, like cognitive abilities or even certain predispositions toward specific types of intelligence or temperament traits. \n\nCould you elaborate on what the research says regarding more specific biological differences, like variations in processing speed, spatial reasoning, or even impulse control, across different ancestral groups? Is there any consensus on how these might be linked to genetic differences?",
